/-!
# Painlevé–Gullstrand: the atom `q = √(2M/r)` and its derivative shapes

The only analytic input of the PG tables beyond `Atlas.Core.Deriv`: for `M ≥ 0`, `r > 0`,
`q² = 2M/r` and `q' = −q/(2r)` (genuine `HasDerivAt`, including the case `M = 0` where `q ≡ 0`).
The shape lemmas in `PG.D` certify the closed forms that occur in the Christoffel table.
